# Manual exploration with the VS Code REST Client (or JetBrains HTTP client).
# Start the API first: `pnpm db:up && pnpm start:dev`, or `docker compose up --build`.
# The expected results assume no bookings yet: run `pnpm db:reset` (or
# `docker compose down -v`) first, since ids are never reused.
# Times are plain integers; here 900 reads as 9:00 just for readability.
@api = http://localhost:3000

### Resources
GET {{api}}/resources

### Book ROOM-A for [900, 915)
POST {{api}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "daily", "resourceId": "ROOM-A", "start": 29895240, "end": 29895300 }

### Adjacent booking: starts when "daily" ends → 201
POST {{api}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "retro", "resourceId": "ROOM-A", "start": 29895300, "end": 29895360 }

### Overlap → 409 conflict with ["retro"]
POST {{api}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "planning", "resourceId": "ROOM-A", "start": 29895350, "end": 29895380 }

### Availability without booking
GET {{api}}/resources/ROOM-A/availability?start=29895360&end=29895380

### Cancel (repeat it to get "already_cancelled")
POST {{api}}/bookings/retro/cancellation

### List, optionally filtered by status and resourceId
GET {{api}}/bookings?status=active&resourceId=ROOM-A

### One booking
GET {{api}}/bookings/retro

### Invalid input → 400 validation_error with every invalid field
POST {{api}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": " ", "resourceId": "ROOM-A", "start": 10.5, "end": 5 }
